From 022efe64ab35ed3cf19b1508ac456c7af6c99535 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:15:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] Seer: import Spotify and YouTube Music playlists

Paste a Spotify or YouTube Music playlist/album link, or upload an export
(Exportify CSV, Spotify data JSON, Takeout CSV, "Artist - Title" text).
Songs are matched to MusicBrainz (ISRC, then artist/title/length), missing
ones are requested, and a Navidrome playlist with the same name follows
the downloads. Unmatched songs can be picked by hand, and linked playlists
can be re-read daily. Spotify works without credentials through the embed
page; Seer.Spotify.ClientID/ClientSecret and Seer.YouTube.Cookies unlock
long playlists and private lists.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

